haloed.d:
imp. & p. p. of Halo
a. Surrounded with a halo; invested with an ideal glory;
   glorified.

heaves.d:
n. A disease of horses, characterized by difficult breathing,
   with heaving of the flank, wheezing, flatulency, and a peculiar cough;
   broken wind.

horns.d:
n a noisemaker (as at parties or games) that makes a loud noise when you blow through it
n one of the bony outgrowths on the heads of certain ungulates
n a noise made by the driver of an automobile to give warning;
